{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And there shall be… for the destroyer.</b> Meaning: on account of the destroyer who goes forth to destroy others, he possesses within him only the natural aspect of destruction toward others; but upon seeing the seal of His name, blessed be He — which is the mitzvah — he is terrified and fears to approach him. This is why HaShem commanded that the blood be for a sign. And if you say: if so, an Egyptian who hid himself among the house of Israel would be saved — Scripture teaches: ״בָּכֶם״ — and not among Egyptians, for the light of the mitzvah will not shine for salvation except upon Israel, as it is written (Isaiah 60:2): ״וְעָלַיִךְ יִזְרַח ה׳ וּכְבוֹדוֹ עָלַיִךְ יֵרָאֶה״."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:26:56.033392809Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}